[CL-BUG-094] ## CL-BUG-094 — CRITICAL / P0 — Rust tier: a private method called inside an `if`/`else` branch compiles to `OP_0`
**Dispatcher-verified.** Source: impl-rust-codegen depth NEW-01. Rust tier only — asserted for no other tier.

`lower_if` builds each arm's sub-context and copies back exactly three fields (`compilers/rust/src/codegen/stack.rs:2143-2146`, `:2160-2163`), verified verbatim:
```rust
let mut then_ctx = LoweringContext::new(&[], &self.properties);
then_ctx.sm = self.sm.clone();
then_ctx.outer_protected_refs = Some(protected_refs.clone());
then_ctx.inside_branch = true;
```
`private_methods` is initialised empty in `LoweringContext::new` (`:682`) and populated **only** on the top-level context (`:5364-5367`). It is never copied into an arm. So inside a branch the lookup at `:1917` always misses, control falls to `lower_call`, the name is not a builtin, and execution reaches the catch-all (`:1873-1876`):
```rust
// Unknown function -- push a placeholder
self.emit_op(StackOp::Push(PushValue::Int(BigInt::from(0))));
self.sm.push(binding_name);
return;
```
The helper's body is never emitted, its return value becomes **0**, and — because the N operands were already consumed from the stack *model* at `:1856-1866` — the model and the physical stack desync by the argument count, corrupting every subsequent `OP_PICK`/`OP_ROLL` depth in the method.

Reachable from ordinary valid TypeScript, not just `--ir`: ANF lowering inlines only private methods with state/data outputs (`frontend/anf_lower.rs:921-933`); every other private call is emitted as `MethodCall` and depends entirely on this codegen-side inlining.

